# DTF tier manifest: rubygems-remote-bundler
#   (artifact-keeper#5686, fixed for 1.12.0 by PR #5688)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + the real Ruby/Bundler client
# (client.rubygems, ruby:3.3-slim with Bundler 2.5) + upstreams.mock-files
# (stdlib-python upstream at 172.16.<slot>.76 whose files the oracle writes).
# The oracle builds a small rubygems.org-shaped upstream with the client's own
# `gem` library (fixtures/gen_upstream.rb: real .gem files, quick gemspecs,
# Marshal specs indexes and a Compact Index whose `versions` lines carry the
# MD5 of each `info/<name>` body) and stores it on the mock.
#
# THE BUG
# #5686 A Remote RubyGems repository could not be used as a Bundler source on
#       `/gems/<repo>`. `specs.4.8.gz` and `.gem` files were proxied, but the
#       endpoints Bundler resolves with answered from local rows only: the
#       Compact Index (`/versions`, `/names`, `/info/<name>`) was not routed
#       (404), `quick/Marshal.4.8/<spec>.gemspec.rz` was proxied only for
#       Virtual repositories (404 for any gem a Remote had not cached), and
#       `api/v1/dependencies` answered `200 []`, which reads as "no versions".
#       `bundle lock` / `bundle install` failed. Now a Remote passes the
#       upstream Compact Index and quick gemspecs through byte for byte,
#       re-declaring an upstream Content-Encoding, and its Dependency API
#       answers 404 like rubygems.org.
#
# Oracle (oracle.sh, RELEASE_GATE=1):
#   (FIX)     the Compact Index documents are the upstream bytes and info/<name>
#             matches its MD5 in versions; a gzip-coded info document keeps its
#             Content-Encoding; an uncached quick gemspec is served; the
#             Dependency API does not answer `200 []`; a real `bundle lock` and
#             `bundle install` resolve and install dtfbundler-app 1.0.0 with its
#             dependency through the Remote.
#   (CONTROL) both images: the Remote proxies specs.4.8.gz and a .gem
#             byte for byte; a Local RubyGems repository still answers 404 on
#             the Compact Index (Bundler falls back to the Marshal indexes
#             there, #4272) and still serves its own specs.4.8.gz.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: Bundler issues its resolve requests back to back.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem client.rubygems upstreams.mock-files"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
COVERS="5686"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
